{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"normalized":[{"from":"Warped_Tongs","to":"Warped Tongs"},{"from":"Paper_Krane","to":"Paper Krane"},{"from":"Happy_Flower","to":"Happy Flower"},{"from":"Strange_Spoon","to":"Strange Spoon"},{"from":"Bloody_Idol","to":"Bloody Idol"},{"from":"Holy_Water","to":"Holy Water"},{"from":"Sling_of_Courage","to":"Sling of Courage"},{"from":"The_Courier","to":"The Courier"},{"from":"The_Abacus","to":"The Abacus"},{"from":"Lee's_Waffle","to":"Lee's Waffle"},{"from":"The_Specimen","to":"The Specimen"},{"from":"Wrist_Blade","to":"Wrist Blade"},{"from":"Mark_of_the_Bloom","to":"Mark of the Bloom"},{"from":"The_Boot","to":"The Boot"},{"from":"Twisted_Funnel","to":"Twisted Funnel"},{"from":"Cultist_Headpiece","to":"Cultist Headpiece"},{"from":"Bag_of_Marbles","to":"Bag of Marbles"}],"pages":{"2497":{"pageid":2497,"ns":0,"title":"Bag of Marbles","revisions":[{"revid":56889,"parentid":55633,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Bag of Marbles\n|Image       = BagofMarbles.png\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Description = At the start of each combat, apply 1 {{BD|Vulnerable}} to ALL enemies.\n|Flavor      = A once popular toy in the City. Useful for throwing enemies off balance.\n|GivesToEnemy = Vulnerable\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Vulnerable}}{{R|Bag of Marbles}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|Common:Common|Common}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Small Chest]] or [[Medium Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, {{R|Black Star}}, and {{R|Matryoshka}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Common|Common}} relic can be {{R|Bag of Marbles}}.\n** {{R|Matryoshka}}'s extra relic has a 75% chance of being {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Common|Common}}, which can be {{R|Bag of Marbles}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Bag of Marbles}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Bag of Marbles}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Bag of Marbles}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Bag of Marbles}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Bag of Marbles}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Bag of Marbles}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Bag of Marbles}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Bag of Marbles}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Order ===\n* When calculating damage dealt, all the additive bonuses are added first, and then multiplicative bonuses are multiplied. The final result is rounded down. '''Bag of Marbles'''' {{BD|Vulnerable}} is a multiplicative bonus, and stacks with {{BD|Strength}} and {{BD|Vigor}}.\n* {{R|Bag of Marbles}} will trigger with other \"after opening hand\" relics (such as {{R|Red Mask}} and {{R|Twisted Funnel}}) in pickup order (i.e. from left to right in the player's relic bar).\n\n=== Synergies ===\n\n==== Cards ====\n* {{QueryLink|Cards|Type:Attack|Attacks}} with {{KW|Innate}} (such as {{C|Backstab}} or {{C|Mind Blast}}) or any powerful {{QueryLink|Cards|Type:Attack|attack}} bottled with {{R|Bottled Flame}} (such as {{C|Bludgeon}} or {{C|Sunder}}) can reliably benefit from the {{BD|Vulnerable}} on turn 1.\n* Powerful {{QueryLink|Cards|Type:Attack|attacks}} that damage all enemies (such as {{C|Immolate}}, {{C|Whirlwind}}, {{C|Hyperbeam}}, or {{C|Conclude}}) can be highly effective at dealing with combats that have multiple low-health enemies.\n* Cards that provide cheap damage mitigation (such as {{C|Boot Sequence}}, or {{C|Piercing Wail}}) can make it safer and easier to spend more {{KW|Energy}} on playing {{QueryLink|Cards|Type:Attack|attacks}}.\n\n==== Relics ====\n* The {{BD|Vigor}} provided by {{R|Akabeko}} benefits from {{BD|Vulnerable}}'s damage bonus.\n* Also applies {{BD|Weak}} if the player has {{R|Champion Belt}} (and the {{BD|Vulnerable}} isn't initially blocked by {{BD|Artifact}}).\n* The three {{C|Shiv|Shivs}} from {{R|Ninja Scroll}} can reliably take advantage of the {{BD|Vulnerable}} on turn 1.\n* Relics that provide additional {{BD|Strength}} at the start of combat (such as {{R|Vajra}}, {{R|Girya}}, or {{R|Mutagenic Strength}}) can be further multiplied by the {{BD|Vulnerable}} for each attack played on turn 1.\n* Relics that provide damage mitigation on turn 1 (such as {{R|Anchor}} or {{R|Incense Burner}} if timed correctly) can make it safer and easier to spend more {{KW|Energy}} on playing {{QueryLink|Cards|Type:Attack|attacks}}.\n* Relics that provide additional {{KW|Energy}} on turn 1 (such as {{R|Lantern}} or {{R|Ancient Tea Set}}) can make it easier to play more {{QueryLink|Cards|Type:Attack|attacks}}.\n* Relics that provide additional card draw on turn 1 (such as {{R|Bag of Preparation}} or {{R|Snecko Eye}}) can make it easier to draw more (or better) {{QueryLink|Cards|Type:Attack|attacks}} to play.\n** {{R|Gambling Chip}} can be used to discard unneeded {{QueryLink|Cards|Type:Skill|skills}} or {{QueryLink|Cards|Type:Power|powers}} on turn 1 to potentially draw into more {{QueryLink|Cards|Type:Attack|attacks}} instead.\n\n==== Potions ====\n* The added {{BD|Strength}} from {{P|Strength Potion}} and {{P|Flex Potion}} benefits from {{BD|Vulnerable}}'s damage bonus.\n* The free {{QueryLink|Cards|Type:Attack|attack}} chosen from {{P|Attack Potion}} can benefit from {{BD|Vulnerable}}'s damage bonus while requiring no {{KW|Energy}} to play.\n* The additional {{KW|Energy}} from {{P|Energy Potion}} can make it easier to play more (or better) {{QueryLink|Cards|Type:Attack|attacks}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Removes 1 {{BD|Artifact}} from enemies that start combat with some applied, such as the {{M|Sentry|Sentries}} or {{M|Spheric Guardian}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* Too many {{KW|Innate}} {{QueryLink|Cards|Type:Skill|skills}} or {{QueryLink|Cards|Type:Power|powers}} can make it less likely to draw into {{QueryLink|Cards|Type:Attack|attacks}} before the {{BD|Vulnerable}} disappears.\n* The {{BD|Weak}} from {{R|Gremlin Visage}} is the antithesis to the {{BD|Vulnerable}} from {{R|Bag of Marbles}}, making the damage bonus less effective.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"3136":{"pageid":3136,"ns":0,"title":"Bloody Idol","revisions":[{"revid":55657,"parentid":51006,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Bloody Idol\n|Image       = BloodyIdol.png\n|Rarity      = Event\n|Source      = Forgotten Altar\n|Description = Whenever you gain [[Gold]], heal 5 HP.\n|Flavor      = The idol now weeps a constant stream of blood.\n}}\n{{R|Bloody Idol}} is an {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Event|Event}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\nCan only be obtained from {{E|Forgotten Altar}} by selecting the {{Frame|Offer: Golden Idol}} option. {{R|Golden Idol}} must first be obtained from the [[Event]] with the same name; {{E|Golden Idol}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n{{R|Bloody Idol}} works with ''any'' source of [[Gold]], including [[Gold]] gained from [[Chests]], [[Cards]], [[Relics]], and [[Events]].\n\n=== Synergies ===\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Wish}} can give 25 (30) [[Gold]] via the {{C|Fame and Fortune}} option.\n* {{C|Hand of Greed}} gives 20 (25) [[Gold]] when killing any non-{{BD|Minion}} enemy.\n\n==== Relics ====\n* {{R|Ceramic Fish}} gives 9 [[Gold]] and heals 5 HP whenever the player permanently adds a card to their deck.\n* {{R|Maw Bank}} gives 12 [[Gold]] and heals 5 HP every floor until an item is bought at the [[Merchant]].\n* {{R|Old Coin}} gives 300 [[Gold]] and heals 5 HP on pickup.\n* {{R|Tiny House}} gives 50 [[Gold]] and heals 5 HP on pickup.\n* {{R|Ssserpent Head}} gives 50 [[Gold]] and heals 5 HP whenever a [[Map Locations#Unknown|? room]] is entered.\n* {{R|Magic Flower}} can increase the healing from specifically {{C|Hand of Greed}} and {{C|Wish}} (only healing ''during combat'' is affected). This allows {{R|Bloody Idol}} to heal the player for 8 HP instead of the usual 5 HP.\n** There is also the very niche scenario where the player possesses {{R|Ceramic Fish}} and a card is added to their deck during combat (the {{C|Parasite}} from {{M|Writhing Mass}}' {{Int|Writhing Mass|Parasite}}).\n\n==== Events ====\n* {{E|Knowing Skull}} can be ''incredibly'' powerful with {{R|Bloody Idol}}. Its {{Frame|Riches?}} option will cost the player HP in exchange for [[Gold]], which in turn will cause the player to heal most of the damage taken using {{R|Bloody Idol}}. This can allow the player to earn ''significantly'' more [[Gold]] while also keeping any HP lost to a far more manageable level.\n** This combo is even stronger if the player also possesses {{R|Tungsten Rod}}.\n* {{E|Face Trader}} can give 75 ({{Asc|15|50}}) [[Gold]] in exchange for taking damage equal to 10% of the player's Max HP via the {{Frame|Touch}} option. {{R|Bloody Idol}} can help offset the damage taken from this option. The event can also give {{R|Ssserpent Head}} via the {{Frame|Trade}} option.\n* There are too many other [[Events]] that simply give [[Gold]] in benign ways to list here; the ones listed above have interactions with {{R|Bloody Idol}} that are significant enough to list here explicitly. For a full list of all events where gaining gold is possible, see [[Gold#Events|Gold > Events]].\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As with all healing effects, the healing from {{R|Bloody Idol}} restores no HP if the player possesses {{R|Mark of the Bloom}}.\n* {{R|Ectoplasm}} prevents {{R|Bloody Idol}} from triggering as no [[Gold]] can be gained from any source.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Hand of Greed card now gives gold instantly, rather than through VFX (triggered Bloody Idol).\n* '''Weekly Patch 32: Face Trader'''\n** Knowing Skull HP cost minimum is set to 6 to prevent infinite gold with Bloody Idol.\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Replacing relics now retains the array order, fixing Bloody Idol + Black Blood issue.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"3127":{"pageid":3127,"ns":0,"title":"Cultist Headpiece","revisions":[{"revid":51007,"parentid":50982,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Cultist Headpiece\n|Image       = CultistMask.png\n|Rarity      = Event\n|Source      = Face Trader\n|Description = You feel more talkative.\n|Flavor      = Part of the Flock!\n}}\n{{R|Cultist Headpiece}} is an {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Event|Event}} [[Relic]]. It has no mechanical benefit, and only causes the player's character to yell \"{{TS||shake|CAW! CAAW}}\" at the start of each combat.\n\n== Sources ==\nCan only be obtained from {{E|Face Trader}} by selecting the {{Frame|Trade}} option and randomly receiving {{R|Cultist Headpiece}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Cultist Headpiece}} can be safely traded for {{R|N'loth's Gift}} if it's randomly chosen in the {{E|N'loth}} [[Event]] since it has no mechanical benefit.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Internally called <code>CultistMask</code>.\n* {{R|Cultist Headpiece}} is the face of a {{M|Cultist}} that was taken by the {{E|Face Trader}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** Face Trader event will no longer give out duplicate relics on Endless mode.\n* '''Weekly Patch 32: Face Trader'''\n** Adding event relic Cultist Headpiece.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"2565":{"pageid":2565,"ns":0,"title":"Duality","revisions":[{"revid":55753,"parentid":55419,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Duality\n|Image       = Duality.png\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Character   = Watcher\n|Description = Whenever you play an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}}, gain 1 temporary {{BD|Dexterity}}.\n|Flavor      = \"And the sun was extinguished forever, as if curtains fell before it.\" - Zoroth\n}} \n{{Power Infobox|Dexterity}} {{Power Infobox|Dexterity Down}}\n{{R|Duality}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|character:Watcher|Watcher-exclusive}} {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} [[Relic]]. After an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} has been played and finishes resolving its effect, {{R|Duality}} will apply 1 {{BD|Dexterity}} and 1 {{BD|Dexterity Down}} to the player.\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, {{R|Black Star}}, and {{R|Matryoshka}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic can be {{R|Duality}}.\n** {{R|Matryoshka}}'s extra relic has a 25% chance of being {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}}, which can be {{R|Duality}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Duality}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Duality}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Duality}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Duality}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Duality}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Duality}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Duality}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Colosseum}}: The {{Frame|VICTORY}} option drops 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic (which can be {{R|Duality}}), and 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic.\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Duality}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n\n== Spawn Restrictions ==\n* Can only be obtained by [[Watcher]].\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Order ===\n* When playing an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} that also grants {{KW|Block}} (such as {{C|Iron Wave}}), the {{KW|Block}} will be granted before the {{BD|Dexterity}} is applied. {{R|Duality}} will, somewhat deceptively, flash to indicate it has been triggered before the card is played however.\n* {{BD|Dexterity Down}}, much like {{BD|Strength Down}}, behaves somewhat unintuitively with {{BD|Artifact}}.\n** If the {{BD|Artifact}} is applied ''before'' an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} triggers adding the {{BD|Dexterity}} and {{BD|Dexterity Down}}, then the {{BD|Artifact}} is consumed by blocking the {{BD|Dexterity Down}} and the player is left with 1 normal {{BD|Dexterity}} that lasts for the remainder of the fight.\n** If one or more {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}} trigger adding the {{BD|Dexterity Down}} and then {{BD|Artifact}} is applied ''afterwards'', the {{BD|Artifact}} is consumed at the end of the current turn when the {{BD|Dexterity Down}} would trigger and prevents it from reducing the player's {{BD|Dexterity}}. The '''Dexterity Down''' is still removed from the player as normal when this happens. The player is left with however much {{BD|Dexterity}} they've accumulated so far, which now lasts for the remainder of the fight.\n** If the player already has some {{BD|Dexterity Down}}, then gains {{BD|Artifact}}, and then plays another {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} to trigger adding the {{BD|Dexterity}} and {{BD|Dexterity Down}}, then the {{BD|Artifact}} will be consumed immediately and only block the 1 new {{BD|Dexterity Down}}. The rest of the {{BD|Dexterity Down}} that was applied before the {{BD|Artifact}} will still trigger at the end of the turn as normal. The player is left with 1 normal {{BD|Dexterity}} that lasts for the remainder of the fight.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Duality}} can be very powerful when combined with {{R|Orange Pellets}} as it can be relatively easy to stack high amounts of {{BD|Dexterity}} by repeatedly cleansing the temporary {{BD|Dexterity Down}} debuff.\n* {{R|Duality}} works well with effects that allow multiple cheap {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}} to be played in the same turn, such as {{C|Flurry of Blows}}, {{C|Weave}}, and {{C|Blade Dance}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{R|Duality}} is designed after the well-known Yin-Yang symbol from Chinese philosophy.<ref>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yin_and_yang</ref>\n* {{R|Duality}} is internally called <code>Yang</code>.\n<!-- In the game's code: com.megacrit.cardcrawl.relics.deprecated.DEPRECATEDYin -->\n** There is an unused relic in the game's code called <code>Yin</code> which appears to have been the \"opposite\" of <code>Yang</code> ({{R|Duality}}). It would have given the player 1 {{BD|Strength}} and 1 {{BD|Strength Down}} every time they played a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** CONTENT: Watcher only, Uncommon Relic: Duality\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"2382":{"pageid":2382,"ns":0,"title":"Girya","revisions":[{"revid":55800,"parentid":50882,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Girya\n|Image       = Girya.png\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Description = You can now gain {{BD|Strength}} at Rest Sites (up to 3 times).\n|Flavor      = This Girya is unfathomably heavy. You could train with this to get significantly stronger.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Strength}}{{R|Girya}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} [[Relic]]. It adds a \"Lift\" option to [[Map Locations#Rest Sites|Rest Sites]]. After using Lift, {{R|Girya}} will grant the player 1 {{BD|Strength}} at the start of every combat. Lift may be used up to 3 times total, granting up to 3 {{BD|Strength}}, and then the Lift option will be disabled.\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Medium Chest]] or [[Large Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}} and {{R|Shovel}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic can be {{R|Girya}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Girya}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Girya}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Girya}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Girya}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Girya}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Girya}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Girya}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Colosseum}}: The {{Frame|VICTORY}} option drops 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic, and 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic (which can be {{R|Girya}}).\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Girya}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n** {{E|Mind Bloom}}: The {{Frame|I Am War}} option can drop {{R|Girya}}.\n** {{E|Mysterious Sphere}}: The {{Frame|Open Sphere}} option can drop {{R|Girya}}.\n\n== Spawn Restrictions ==\n* Can only be obtained below floor 49 (the last [[Rest Site]] before the [[Bosses#Act_3_Bosses|Act 3 Boss]]).\n* Only '''two''' relics that add an option to [[Rest Site|Rest Sites]] ({{R|Girya}}, {{R|Peace Pipe}}, and {{R|Shovel}}) can be offered to the player during a run. Once two have been offered, the third will no longer be accessible by any means.\n* {{R|Black Star}}'s extra relic can never drop a relic that adds an option to [[Rest Site|Rest Sites]] (like {{R|Girya}}).\n\n== Interactions ==\nThe {{BD|Strength}} is provided by {{R|Girya}} itself at the start of each combat. If {{R|Girya}} is lost (such as by trading it in the {{E|N'loth}} event), the {{BD|Strength}} will also be lost.\n\n=== Order ===\nWhen calculating damage dealt, all the additive bonuses are added first, and then multiplicative bonuses are multiplied. The final result is rounded down. {{R|Girya}}'s {{BD|Strength}} is an additive bonus.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{BD|Strength}} is applied to each hit in an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|attack}}, allowing multi-hit {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|attacks}} (such as {{C|Sword Boomerang}}, {{C|Flechettes}}, {{C|Barrage}}, and {{C|Bowling Bash}}) to benefit from {{BD|Strength}} multiple times.\n* {{C|Heavy Blade}} specifically benefits from {{BD|Strength}} multiple times in its effect, even though it's a single-hit {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|attack}}.\n* {{C|Reaper}}'s healing increases based on its unblocked damage, and therefore more {{BD|Strength}} will cause it to heal more HP.\n* {{C|Wallop}}'s {{KW|Block}} gain increases based on its unblocked damage, and therefore more {{BD|Strength}} will cause it to gain more {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Limit Break}} can be used to multiply the player's current {{BD|Strength}}.\n* {{R|Girya}}'s '''Lift''' option can be provide the player with something to do at [[Rest Site|Rest Sites]] if they do not have any particularly good {{KW|Upgrade|Upgrades}} to '''Smith''' and they're comfortable with their amount of HP and don't need to '''Rest'''.\n** Also applicable if the player has {{R|Fusion Hammer}} and/or {{R|Coffee Dripper}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The word \"girya\" is a Russian term for a [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kettlebell kettlebell], a type of spherical metal exercise weight with a handle opposite its flat bottom.\n** Russian girya are traditionally measured using a weight unit called [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pood pood], which equates to roughly 16 kg or roughly 36 lbs. {{R|Girya}}'s flavor text mentions that it is ''\"unfathomably heavy\"'', and likely weighs much more than this.\n* {{R|Girya}} depicts a frowning face on the side of it. Real-world girya typically depict their weight measured in kilograms or pounds instead.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 52: Release Date Price Increase'''\n** Fixed issue that caused Shovel, Girya, and Peace Pipe to incorrectly spawn when they should not.\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Girya relic no longer spawns beyond floor 48 (excludes Endless mode).\n* '''Weekly Patch 47: Metamorphosis'''\n** Relics with counters like Pen Nib and Girya no longer display the counter offset incorrectly when the player has too many relics.\n* '''Weekly Patch 30: Skewer'''\n** Updated asset for Lift option via Girya.\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Wording: Campfire -> Rest Site for Girya and Peace Pipe.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"2512":{"pageid":2512,"ns":0,"title":"Happy Flower","revisions":[{"revid":50810,"parentid":37178,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Happy Flower\n|Image       = HappyFlower.png\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Description = Every 3 turns, gain 1 {{KW|Energy}}.\n|Flavor      = This unceasingly joyous plant is a popular novelty item among nobles.\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Energy}}{{R|Happy Flower}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Common|Common}} [[Relic]]. The counter that keeps track of how many turns have passed is not reset between combats, and it's incremented at the ''start'' of the player's turn. This means that if the counter is at 2 at the end of a combat, it will trigger at the start of the next combat and reset to 0 as normal.\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Small Chest]] or [[Medium Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, {{R|Black Star}}, and {{R|Matryoshka}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Common|Common}} relic can be {{R|Happy Flower}}.\n** {{R|Matryoshka}}'s extra relic has a 75% chance of being {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Common|Common}}, which can be {{R|Happy Flower}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Happy Flower}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Happy Flower}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Happy Flower}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Happy Flower}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Happy Flower}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Happy Flower}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Happy Flower}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Happy Flower}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The art for {{R|Happy Flower}} is a direct reference to the Sunflower from the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plants%20vs.%20Zombies Plants vs. Zombies series].\n* The name \"Happy Flower\" itself could also be a reference to the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paper_Mario Paper Mario series] in which there is an equip-able [https://www.mariowiki.com/Happy_Flower_(badge) badge of the same name] with a somewhat similar effect.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"1526":{"pageid":1526,"ns":0,"title":"Holy Water","revisions":[{"revid":56353,"parentid":55442,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Relic Infobox\n| Name        = Holy Water\n| Image       = HolyWater.png\n| Rarity      = Boss\n| Character   = Watcher\n| Description = Replaces {{R|Pure Water}}. At the start of each combat, add 3 {{C|Miracle|Miracles}} into your hand.\n| Flavor      = Collected from a time before the Spire.\n}}\n{{Small Card Infobox|Miracle}}{{R|Holy Water}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|character:Watcher|Watcher-exclusive}} {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Boss|Boss}} [[Relic]]. It's the upgraded form of {{R|Pure Water}}, and replaces it entirely when acquired from a Boss Chest.\n\n== Sources ==\nCan only be obtained as a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Boss|Boss Relic}} choice, if the player has {{R|Pure Water}}.\n\n== Spawn Restrictions ==\n* Can only be obtained by [[Watcher]] while they possess {{R|Pure Water}}.\n* Can never be obtained from [[Boss Swap]].\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Miracle}} is a convenient trigger for {{C|Crush Joints}} and {{C|Sanctity}}.\n* {{C|Miracle}} can be used on-demand to increase the effectiveness of X-cost cards (such as {{C|Collect}} and {{C|Conjure Blade}}).\n* {{C|Miracle}} is a fully reliable +1 to the counter for {{R|Ink Bottle}} every combat.\n* Increases {{KW|Block}} gained by {{R|Cloak Clasp}} and {{C|Spirit Shield}} while {{C|Miracle}}s are {{KW|Retain|retained}}.\n* Generates a card from {{R|Dead Branch}} when a {{C|Miracle}} is played, potentially being able to use the extra {{Icon|PE}}[[Keywords#Energy|energy]] to play the card that generated.\n* {{R|Ice Cream}} can preserve the {{Icon|PE}}[[Keywords#Energy|energy]] from the {{C|Miracle}} between turns without clogging the hand from too many {{KW|Retain}} cards.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Most forms of creating {{C|Miracle}}s happen at the start of combat or enter the hand already {{KW|Upgrade|upgraded}} (in the case of {{C|Collect}}), making {{C|Master Reality}} not as useful for '''Miracles''' as it may seem at first.\n\n=== Anti-Synergy ===\n* It can be awkward to play {{C|Miracle}}s for {{Icon|PE}}[[Keywords#Energy|energy]] while {{R|Velvet Choker}} limits the number of cards that can be played in a turn.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** CONTENT: Watcher only, Boss Relic: Holy Water\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"3151":{"pageid":3151,"ns":0,"title":"Lee's Waffle","revisions":[{"revid":50962,"parentid":37189,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Lee's Waffle\n|Image       = LeesWaffle.png\n|Rarity      = Shop\n|Description = Upon pickup, raise your Max HP by 7 and heal all of your HP.\n|Flavor      = \"Tastiest treat you will find in all the Spire! Baked today just for you.\"\n}}\n{{R|Lee's Waffle}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Shop|Shop}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can only be bought from the [[Merchant]]. Only 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Shop|Shop Relic}} is available per [[Shop]], even with {{R|The Courier}}, since it cannot restock Shop Relics.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Since {{R|Lee's Waffle}} already heals all of the player's HP, it is one of the few healing effects which does not benefit from {{R|Magic Flower}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As with all healing effects, {{R|Lee's Waffle}} restores no HP if the player possesses {{R|Mark of the Bloom}}.\n** Gaining more Max HP is mostly worthless if the player has {{R|Mark of the Bloom}} which prevents all healing. It also prevents the behavior where gaining Max HP will restore HP equal to the amount of Max HP gained.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{R|Lee's Waffle}} is a reference to a friend of the developers named Lee, who had a waffle machine at work. ''(citation needed)''\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 25: Building Blocks'''\n** HP-gain relics (Fruit & Waffle) now have consistent pickup wording.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"3142":{"pageid":3142,"ns":0,"title":"Mark of the Bloom","revisions":[{"revid":51023,"parentid":50988,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Mark of the Bloom\n|Image       = MarkoftheBloom.png\n|Rarity      = Event\n|Source      = Mind Bloom\n|Description = You can no longer heal.\n|Flavor      = In the Beyond, thoughts and reality are one.\n}}\n{{R|Mark of the Bloom}} is an {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Event|Event}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\nCan only be obtained from {{E|Mind Bloom}} by selecting the {{Frame|I am Awake}} option.\n\n== Interactions ==\n{{R|Mark of the Bloom}} truly does prevent '''ALL''' forms of healing, including effects which are not obviously described as healing (such as the behavior where gaining Max HP will restore HP equal to the amount of Max HP gained). The following effects are considered healing and are therefore prevented by {{R|Mark of the Bloom}}:\n\n==== Map Locations ====\n* Resting at a [[Map Locations#Rest Sites|Rest Site]].\n* The automatic healing from transitioning between [[Acts]].\n\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Feed}} (only the heal)\n* {{C|Reaper}}\n* {{C|Self Repair}}\n* {{C|Bandage Up}}\n* {{C|Bite}}\n\n==== Relics ====\n* {{R|Burning Blood}} and {{R|Black Blood}}\n* {{R|Blood Vial}}\n* {{R|Meal Ticket}}\n* {{R|Regal Pillow}}\n* {{R|Strawberry}} (only the heal)\n* {{R|Toy Ornithopter}}\n* {{R|Darkstone Periapt}} (only the heal)\n* {{R|Eternal Feather}}\n* {{R|Meat on the Bone}}\n* {{R|Pantograph}}\n* {{R|Pear}} (only the heal)\n* {{R|Singing Bowl}} (only the heal)\n* {{R|Bird-Faced Urn}}\n* {{R|Lizard Tail}} (cannot heal the player on death, and will not be consumed to save their life)\n* {{R|Magic Flower}} (does not heal the player directly, but its healing multiplier is made useless)\n* {{R|Mango}} (only the heal)\n* {{R|Tiny House}} (only the heal)\n* {{R|Lee's Waffle}} (only the heal)\n* {{R|Bloody Idol}}\n* {{R|Face of Cleric}} (only the heal)\n\n==== Events ====\n* {{E|Bonfire Spirits}} (the healing from removing a non-{{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Basic|Basic}} card)\n* {{E|Big Fish}} (the healing from the {{Frame|Banana}} option, and the healing from gaining Max HP by the {{Frame|Donut}} option)\n* {{E|Hypnotizing Colored Mushrooms}} (the healing from the {{Frame|Eat}} option)\n* {{E|The Cleric}} (the healing from the {{Frame|Heal}} option)\n* {{E|Forgotten Altar}} (the healing from gaining Max HP by the {{Frame|Sacrifice}} option)\n* {{E|The Library}} (the healing from the {{Frame|Sleep}} option)\n* {{E|Mind Bloom}} (the healing from the {{Frame|I am Healthy}} option; only possible in [[Endless]] mode if the player encounters this [[Event]] a second time)\n* {{E|The Moai Head}} (the healing from the {{Frame|Jump Inside}} option)\n* {{E|Winding Halls}} (the healing from the {{Frame|Pass On}} option)\n\n==== Potions ====\n* {{P|Blood Potion}}\n* {{P|Fairy in a Bottle}} (cannot heal the player on death, and will not be consumed to save their life)\n* {{P|Fruit Juice}} (only the heal)\n* {{P|Regen Potion}}\n\n== Trivia ==\n* There is a \"Wall of Shame\" on [https://www.reddit.com/r/slaythespire/ the official Slay the Spire subreddit] that tracks the last time someone was caught off-guard by how many healing-like effects are prevented by {{R|Mark of the Bloom}} (particularly from {{R|Lizard Tail}} and {{P|Fairy in a Bottle}}).<ref>https://www.reddit.com/r/slaythespire/comments/yackge/no_its_not_a_bug_the_mark_of_the_bloom_wall_of/</ref>\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Update 36: Power Through'''\n** Fixed an incorrect interaction with Mark of the Bloom and the Moai Head event in Act 3.\n* '''Weekly Patch 28: The Ritual'''\n** New Relic: Mark of the Bloom\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"1803":{"pageid":1803,"ns":0,"title":"Paper Krane","revisions":[{"revid":56369,"parentid":55889,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n| Name        = Paper Krane\n| Image       = PaperCrane.png\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Character   = Silent\n| Description = Enemies with {{BD|Weak}} deal 40% less damage rather than 25%.\n| Flavor      = An origami of a creature from a past age.\n| InteractsWith = Weak\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Weak}}\n{{R|Paper Krane}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|character:Silent|Silent-exclusive}} {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} [[Relic]]. It further decreases how much Damage enemies with {{BD|Weak}} will deal. Enemies with {{BD|Weak}} will deal 40% less damage, rounding down, rather than 25% less damage.\n\nEnemy [[Intent]] will always show the correct amount of damage an enemy with {{BD|Weak}} will deal (except for some specific damage numbers in [[Elites|Spire Elites]]).\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, {{R|Black Star}}, and {{R|Matryoshka}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic can be {{R|Paper Krane}}.\n** {{R|Matryoshka}}'s extra relic has a 25% chance of being {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}}, which can be {{R|Paper Krane}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Paper Krane}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Paper Krane}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Paper Krane}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Paper Krane}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Paper Krane}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Paper Krane}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Paper Krane}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Colosseum}}: The {{Frame|VICTORY}} option drops 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic (which can be {{R|Paper Krane}}), and 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic.\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Paper Krane}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n\n== Spawn Restrictions ==\n* Can only be obtained by [[Silent]].\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Anything that applies {{BD|Weak}} to enemies will be more effective with {{R|Paper Krane}}:\n\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Neutralize}}\n* {{C|Sucker Punch}}\n* {{C|Crippling Cloud}}\n* {{C|Leg Sweep}}\n* {{C|Malaise}}\n* {{C|Blind}}\n\nThe following cards can benefit from {{R|Paper Krane}} if acquired from another character, such as via {{R|Prismatic Shard}}:\n\n* {{C|Clothesline}}\n* {{C|Intimidate}}\n* {{C|Shockwave}}\n* {{C|Uppercut}}\n* {{C|Go for the Eyes}}\n* {{C|Sash Whip}}\n* {{C|Wave of the Hand}}\n\n==== Relics ====\n* {{R|Red Mask}}\n* Theoretically {{R|Champion Belt}}, but that is an [[Ironclad]]-exclusive relic while {{R|Paper Krane}} is [[Silent]]-exclusive. It is not possible to obtain both relics during normal gameplay, even with {{R|Prismatic Shard}} as it only affects card rewards.\n\n==== Potions ====\n* {{P|Weak Potion}}\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{R|Paper Krane}}, just like {{R|Paper Phrog}}, is an example of ''Origami''; the Japanese art of folding paper into recognizable objects.<ref>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Origami</ref> A paper crane in particular is one of the most common origami models.\n* In Japanese tradition and ancient folklore, it is believed that folding 1000 paper cranes will perform miracles or provide good fortune to people in need, such as bringing peace to warring nations or curing illnesses.<ref>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/One_thousand_origami_cranes</ref>\n* It is not known why the relic's name is spelled ''Krane'' instead of the correct spelling of ''Crane''.\n* Internally called <code>Paper Crane</code>.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 38: Bane'''\n* Paper Krane relic nerf: 50% -> 40% damage reduction.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"3122":{"pageid":3122,"ns":0,"title":"Pocketwatch","revisions":[{"revid":55899,"parentid":50889,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Pocketwatch\n|Image       = Pocketwatch.png\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Description = Whenever you play 3 or less cards during your turn, draw 3 additional cards at the start of your next turn.\n|Flavor      = The hands seem stuck on the 3 o'clock position.\n|Keywords    = Draw\n}}\n{{R|Pocketwatch}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Medium Chest]] or [[Large Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, and {{R|Black Star}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic can be {{R|Pocketwatch}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Pocketwatch}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Pocketwatch}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Pocketwatch}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Pocketwatch}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Pocketwatch}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Pocketwatch}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Pocketwatch}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Colosseum}}: The {{Frame|VICTORY}} option drops 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic, and 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic (which can be {{R|Pocketwatch}}).\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Pocketwatch}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n** {{E|Mind Bloom}}: The {{Frame|I Am War}} option can drop {{R|Pocketwatch}}.\n** {{E|Mysterious Sphere}}: The {{Frame|Open Sphere}} option can drop {{R|Pocketwatch}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Pocketwatch}} works well with decks that have a fair amount of high-cost cards with impactful effects to help reduce the number of cards that need to be played each turn (such as {{C|Immolate}}, {{C|Crippling Cloud}}, {{C|Glacier}}, and {{C|Wallop}}).\n* Even in decks that can't make effective use of high-cost cards, it can still be beneficial to skip playing cards that have little impact on the outcome of a fight, such as {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Basic&search:Strike|basic Strikes}} and other low damage {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}} to make it more likely that they will draw into better cards next turn.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Effects that limit cards played (such as {{R|Velvet Choker}}, {{C|Normality}}, or {{M|Time Eater}}'s {{BD|Time Warp}}) will naturally steer the player into playing fewer cards. {{R|Pocketwatch}} can help the player manage these otherwise severe debuffs by making it more likely they draw the cards they need each turn.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* Decks that rely on playing many cards will struggle to make use of {{R|Pocketwatch}}. Examples include:\n** Infinite combo decks, such as ones that rely on {{R|Sundial}} or {{C|Nightmare}}.\n** Decks with many cheap cards, which may rely on effects like {{C|All for One}} and {{R|Unceasing Top}} to quickly play lots of cards each turn.\n** Decks that are already able to effectively draw cards without needing to limit their card plays (such as using {{C|Dark Embrace}}, {{C|Acrobatics}}, {{C|Coolheaded}}, and {{C|Rushdown}}).\n* Cards which generate or fetch other cards (such as {{C|Infernal Blade}}, {{C|Blade Dance}}, {{C|Seek}}, and {{C|Foreign Influence}}) will use multiple card plays and make it more difficult to trigger {{R|Pocketwatch}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* It would be more grammatically correct for {{R|Pocketwatch}}'s description to say ''3 or fewer cards'' instead of ''3 or less cards''.<ref>https://www.merriam-webster.com/grammar/fewer-vs-less</ref>\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** Fixed Pocketwatch relic activating too early for effects like Foresight.\n* '''Weekly Patch 41: Chill'''\n** New Rare Relic: Pocketwatch.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"3150":{"pageid":3150,"ns":0,"title":"Sling of Courage","revisions":[{"revid":55615,"parentid":50970,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Sling of Courage\n|Image       = Sling.png\n|Rarity      = Shop\n|Description = Start each Elite combat with 2 {{BD|Strength}}.\n|Flavor      = A handy tool for dealing with particularly tough opponents.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Strength}}{{R|Sling of Courage}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Shop|Shop}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can only be bought from the [[Merchant]]. Only 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Shop|Shop Relic}} is available per [[Shop]], even with {{R|The Courier}}, since it cannot restock Shop Relics.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Preserved Insect}} will make [[Elites]] easier to kill by reducing their HP by 25%.\n* {{R|Black Star}} drops an extra [[Relic]] after winning an [[Elite]] combat, making these fights more rewarding.\n* {{R|Slaver's Collar}} grants the player 1 additional {{KW|Energy}} in [[Elite]] combats, and can allow the player to kill [[Elites]] more easily.\n* {{BD|Strength}} is applied to each hit in an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|attack}}, allowing multi-hit {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|attacks}} (such as {{C|Sword Boomerang}}, {{C|Flechettes}}, {{C|Barrage}}, and {{C|Bowling Bash}}) to benefit from  {{BD|Strength}} multiple times.\n* {{C|Heavy Blade}} specifically benefits from {{BD|Strength}} multiple times in its effect, even though it's a single-hit {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|attack}}.\n* {{C|Reaper}}'s healing increases based on its unblocked damage, and therefore more {{BD|Strength}} will cause it to heal more HP.\n* {{C|Wallop}}'s {{KW|Block}} gain increases based on its unblocked damage, and therefore more {{BD|Strength}} will cause it to gain more {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Limit Break}} can be used to multiply the player's current {{BD|Strength}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* A sling is a type of simple primitive weapon made from rope which used to propel a blunt object (such as a stone or lead \"sling bullet\") at higher speeds and greater distances than if the user attempted to throw the object by hand to the best of their ability.<ref>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sling_(weapon)</ref>\n* {{R|Sling of Courage}} is a reference to the Biblical story of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David David] and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goliath Goliath]. In the story, David is tasked to kill the Philistine giant Goliath in single combat, and he succeeds by using a [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sling_(weapon)#Biblical_accounts sling] to slay his opponent in a single strike to their head.<ref>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goliath#Biblical_accounts</ref>\n* Internally called <code>Sling</code>.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 46: Adrenaline'''\n** Preserved Insect and Sling should now work in all elite combats including elite battles from events (like dead adventurer event).\n* '''Weekly Patch 35: Aggregate'''\n** Sling Of Courage relic was incorrectly flashing in every room.\n* '''Weekly Patch 33: Terror'''\n** Adding relic Sling of Courage.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"3153":{"pageid":3153,"ns":0,"title":"Strange Spoon","revisions":[{"revid":50971,"parentid":37264,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Strange Spoon\n|Image       = StrangeSpoon.png\n|Rarity      = Shop\n|Description = Cards which {{KW|Exhaust}} when played will instead discard 50% of the time.\n|Flavor      = Staring at the spoon, it appears to bend and twist around before your eyes.\n|Keywords    = Discard\n}}\n{{R|Strange Spoon}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Shop|Shop}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can only be bought from the [[Merchant]]. Only 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Shop|Shop Relic}} is available per [[Shop]], even with {{R|The Courier}}, since it cannot restock Shop Relics.\n\n== Interactions ==\n{{R|Strange Spoon}} specifically only works on cards that ''{{KW|Exhaust}} when played''. The following {{KW|Exhaust}} effects and timings will '''not''' be affected by {{R|Strange Spoon}}:\n* Cards that {{KW|Exhaust}} automatically at the end of the turn because they are {{KW|Ethereal}} (such as {{C|Ghostly Armor}}, {{C|Dazed}}, and {{C|Clumsy}}).\n* Cards that {{KW|Exhaust}} because another effect forces them to (such as cards targeted by {{C|Burning Pact}}, {{C|Fiend Fire}}, and {{P|Elixir}}).\n* Cards that are {{KW|Unplayable}} and {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} by {{C|Havoc}} or {{C|Omniscience}} can never be prevented from {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausting}} because {{KW|Unplayable}} cards can never count as \"being played\".\n* {{C|Deus Ex Machina}} will never be prevented from {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausting}} because it {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} when drawn and does not count as being played.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Strange Spoon}} may cause the 0-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skills}} with {{C|Corruption}} to not {{KW|Exhaust}} when played, allowing them to be played again on a future turn.\n* Some exceptionally powerful cards are somewhat balanced by the fact that they {{KW|Exhaust}} and can normally only be played once per combat. Preventing their removal with {{R|Strange Spoon}} can be quite a powerful effect. Cards such as {{C|Offering}}, {{C|Catalyst}}, {{C|Genetic Algorithm}}, {{C|Vault}}, and {{C|Apparition}} can be played more than once if the player is lucky. \n\n=== Neutral ===\n* The description of {{R|Strange Spoon}} is somewhat misleading in that it will not trigger on-discard effects such as {{R|Hovering Kite}} or {{R|Tingsha}}. Its discard is more similar to the automatic discarding of the player's hand that happens after ending their turn.\n* Cards played by {{C|Havoc}} and {{C|Omniscience}} temporarily gain {{KW|Exhaust}}, and {{R|Strange Spoon}} can prevent these cards from {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausting}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* There are some cards that {{KW|Exhaust}} which the player may not want to re-draw again, such as {{C|Shiv|Shivs}}, {{C|Slimed}}, and {{C|Pride}}.\n* Cards that {{R|Strange Spoon}} prevents from {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausting}} will not trigger {{KW|Exhaust}} synergy effects, such as {{C|Feel No Pain}}, {{C|Dark Embrace}}, and {{R|Dead Branch}}.\n* {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Statuses}} that are made playable and {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} by {{R|Medical Kit}} can be prevented from {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausting}} by {{R|Strange Spoon}}.\n* {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}} that are made playable and {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} by {{R|Blue Candle}} can be prevented from {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausting}} by {{R|Strange Spoon}}. The player will also effectively waste the 1 HP cost from using {{R|Blue Candle}} in this way.\n** This can still be useful in cases such as {{c|Pain}} or {{c|Normality}}, where removing those from one's inventory serves benefit even without exhausting the card.\n\n== Bugs ==\n* If the {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} card from playing {{C|Omniscience}} is prevented from {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausting}} by {{R|Strange Spoon}}, the card will behave as if it has the {{KW|Exhaust}} every time it's played for the rest of combat.<ref>https://www.reddit.com/r/slaythespire/comments/fq5mpx/omniscience_w_spoon_bug/</ref>\n** Despite also temporarily granting {{KW|Exhaust}} to a card, {{C|Havoc}} does not seem to have this bug.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{R|Strange Spoon}} is a reference to [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spoon_bending spoon bending]; a popular magic trick.\n** Popularized by the magician [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uri_Geller Uri Geller], spoon bending has since been associated with having psychokinetic or paranormal abilities.\n** Spoon bending is often referenced in pop culture, such as the famous scene in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Matrix The Matrix] where [https://youtu.be/uAXtO5dMqEI a young boy bends a spoon with his mind and fixes it again] to demonstrate the unreality of their computer simulation, and the evolutionary line of the Psychic-type [https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Pok%C3%A9mon_(species) Pok\u00e9mon] [https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Abra_(Pok%C3%A9mon) Abra], [https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Kadabra_(Pok%C3%A9mon) Kadabra], and [https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Alakazam_(Pok%C3%A9mon) Alakazam], who utilize spoons to amplify their psychokinetic capabilities.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** Fixed Rebound card not working with Strange Spoon relic.\n* '''Weekly Patch 52: Release Date Price Increase'''\n** Updated relic asset for Strange Spoon.\n* '''Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance'''\n** Strange Spoon affects cards exhausted by Medical Kit and Blue Candle now.\n** Strange Spoon is now a shop only relic.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"3154":{"pageid":3154,"ns":0,"title":"The Abacus","revisions":[{"revid":50972,"parentid":37270,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = The Abacus\n|Image       = TheAbacus.png\n|Rarity      = Shop\n|Description = Whenever you shuffle your draw pile, gain 6 {{KW|Block}}.\n|Flavor      = One...Two...Three...\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}}{{R|The Abacus}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Shop|Shop}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can only be bought from the [[Merchant]]. Only 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Shop|Shop Relic}} is available per [[Shop]], even with {{R|The Courier}}, since it cannot restock Shop Relics.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Order ===\n* {{R|The Abacus}} will trigger ''after'' the player has finished drawing cards post-shuffle.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|The Abacus}} can be easier to trigger in smaller decks, or decks that make good use of {{KW|Exhaust}} effects to artificially thin their deck mid-combat (such as from {{C|Burning Pact}} or {{C|Fiend Fire}}, or decks that can draw many cards quite easily (such as by using {{C|Dark Embrace}}, {{C|Calculated Gamble}}, {{C|Heatsinks}}, and {{C|Rushdown}}).\n* {{C|Reboot}} and {{C|Deep Breath}} will trigger {{R|The Abacus}} when they shuffle the player's draw pile. This can be a somewhat consistent way to force a shuffle without needing to draw through the entire draw pile.\n* {{C|Juggernaut}} will deal 5 (7) damage to a random enemy when {{R|The Abacus}} triggers.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n<!-- This section is included in every Relic that triggers \"whenever you shuffle your draw pile\". If you make any changes to this list, please update other relics like Sundial and Melange! -->\n* Effects that say \"''Shuffle a card into your draw pile.''\" do not actually shuffle the draw pile, instead inserting a card into the draw pile in a random position. Therefore, these effects do '''not''' trigger {{R|The Abacus}}:\n** {{C|Wild Strike}}\n** {{C|Reckless Charge}}\n** {{C|Evaluate}}\n** {{C|Pray}}\n** {{C|Reach Heaven}}\n** {{C|Study}}\n** {{C|Tantrum}}\n** {{C|Alpha}}\n** {{C|Conjure Blade}}\n** {{C|Chrysalis}}\n** {{C|Metamorphosis}}\n** {{C|Beta}}\n** {{R|Nilry's Codex}}\n\n== Bugs ==\n* TODO! {{R|The Abacus}} is a ''very'' buggy relic. [[User:Riscuit]] will add more information here.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* An abacus is a hand-operated calculating tool that has been used since ancient times, consisting of a two-dimensional array of slidable beads or stones kept in place by a wooden frame. It's usage is somewhat reminiscent of a more primitive version of a modern calculator.<ref>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abacus</ref>\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 47: Metamorphosis'''\n** Reboot and Deep Breath cards no longer trigger shuffle-based relics twice.\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** Localization: Mutagenic Strength, Meal Ticket, and Abacus now support more flexible descriptions.\n* '''Weekly Patch 32: Face Trader'''\n** Adding shop relic The Abacus.\n\n<!-- Riscuit needs to contribute the bugs, as stated in the Relic Template -->\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:ToUpdate]]\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"2537":{"pageid":2537,"ns":0,"title":"The Boot","revisions":[{"revid":56068,"parentid":55664,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = The Boot\n|Image       = Boot.png\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Description = Whenever you would deal 4 or less unblocked {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} damage, increase it to 5.\n|Flavor      = When wound up, the boot grows larger in size.\n}}\n{{R|The Boot}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|Common:Common|Common}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Small Chest]] or [[Medium Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, {{R|Black Star}}, and {{R|Matryoshka}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Common|Common}} relic can be {{R|The Boot}}.\n** {{R|Matryoshka}}'s extra relic has a 75% chance of being {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Common|Common}}, which can be {{R|The Boot}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|The Boot}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|The Boot}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|The Boot}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|The Boot}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|The Boot}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|The Boot}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|The Boot}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|The Boot}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n* Only damage from {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}} are affected by {{R|The Boot}}. Other damaging effects (such as {{C|Combust}}, {{BD|Poison}}, or {{KW|Lightning}} [[Orbs]]) will not have their damage increased.\n* {{R|The Boot}} will bypass forms of damage reduction (such as the {{M|Byrd|Byrd's}} {{BD|Flying}} and the {{M|Nemesis|Nemesis'}} {{BD|Intangible}}).\n** I.e. playing an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} against an {{BD|Intangible}} {{M|Nemesis}} will deal 5 damage instead of the normal 1 damage.\n* An attack that deals 0 damage after {{BD|Strength}} reduction will still deal 0 damage despite {{R|The Boot}}.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Any card that deals 4 damage or less by default (such as {{C|Reaper}}, {{C|Neutralize}}, {{C|Shiv|Shivs}}, {{C|Barrage}}, and {{C|Flurry of Blows}}) will naturally have their damage increased to 5.\n** This can also extend to slightly higher damage cards whose damage will be below 5 if {{BD|Weak|Weakened}}, such as {{C|Anger}}, {{C|Slice}}, {{C|FTL}}, and {{C|Consecrate}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The visual design of {{R|The Boot}} resembles the Goomba's Shoe (\"Kuribo's Boot\") from the Super Mario Bros. series, making its first appearance in Super Mario Bros. 3.<ref>https://www.mariowiki.com/Goomba's_Shoe</ref>\n* The beta art for {{C|Boot Sequence}} depicts the [[Defect]] inside of {{R|The Boot}}.\n* Internally called <code>Boot</code>.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Fixed Invincible power with interactions such as The Boot and Block.\n* '''Weekly Patch 55: Blur'''\n** '''Reaper card now heals the correct amount if the player has The Boot relic.'''\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** Boot relic now triggers on 4 or less rather than 5, this caused it to flash when it did nothing.\n* '''Weekly Patch 25: Building Blocks'''\n** New common relic The Boot.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"3019":{"pageid":3019,"ns":0,"title":"The Courier","revisions":[{"revid":55406,"parentid":50860,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = The Courier\n|Image       = TheCourier.png\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Description = The Merchant restocks [[Cards|cards]], [[Relics|relics]], and [[Potions|potions]]. All prices are reduced by 20%.\n|Flavor      = The merchant's personal pet!\n}}\n{{R|The Courier}} is an {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} [[Relic]]. When a [[Card]], [[Relic]], or [[Potions|potion]] is purchased from the [[Merchant]], it will immediately be replaced by another item of the same type.\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], or found in a [[Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, {{R|Black Star}}, and {{R|Matryoshka}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic can be {{R|The Courier}}.\n** {{R|Matryoshka}}'s extra relic has a 25% chance of being {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}}, which can be {{R|The Courier}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|The Courier}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|The Courier}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|The Courier}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|The Courier}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|The Courier}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|The Courier}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|The Courier}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Colosseum}}: The {{Frame|VICTORY}} option drops 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic (which can be {{R|The Courier}}), and 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic.\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|The Courier}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n\n== Spawn Restrictions ==\n* Can only be obtained below floor 49 (the last [[Rest Site]] before the [[Bosses#Act_3_Bosses|Act 3 Boss]]).\n* Cannot be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n* Any item re-stocked by {{R|The Courier}} will not be affected by the {{Asc|16|10% price increased}} from Ascension 16+.\n* The [[Merchant]] will only ever stock exactly 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Shop|Shop relic}} on each [[Shop]] floor. If the {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Shop|Shop relic}} is purchased, {{R|The Courier}} will '''not''' replace it with another {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Shop|Shop relic}} and instead replace it with a random {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Common|Common}}, {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}}, or {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic as normal.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* If the player has a high amount of gold (such as from {{R|Old Coin}}, {{E|Mind Bloom}}, or being frugal with the rewards from {{R|Golden Idol}} and {{R|Maw Bank}}), the item-restocking benefit from {{R|The Courier}} can allow them to buy more items than they otherwise could without needing to visit a second [[Merchant]].\n* {{R|The Courier}}'s price reduction stacks with {{R|Membership Card}}; totalling a 60% reduction in the [[Merchant]]'s prices.\n* {{R|The Courier}}'s price reduction will still reduce the price of the card removal service as normal.\n** Some players may forget this fact due to the explicit mention of [[Cards|cards]], [[Relics|relics]], and [[Potions|potions]] in the relic's description with no explicit mention of the card removal service. Price reduction affects ''all'' of the [[Merchant]]'s prices.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{R|Smiling Mask}} will negate {{R|The Courier}}'s price reduction for the card removal service, since it will always be locked at a price of 50 gold. This is not much of a drawback however, as even the cheapest card removal with {{R|The Courier}} will still cost 60 gold without {{R|Smiling Mask}}.\n* {{R|The Courier}}'s price reduction can help stretch a limited [[Gold]] supply if {{R|Ectoplasm}} has been acquired, although its usefulness is heavily limited by being unable to acquire any more [[Gold]].\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{R|The Courier}} is likely a reference to the item of the same name from [https://liquipedia.net/dota2/Courier Dota 2].\n* In runs where the player has seen every [[Relic]] (such as in an [[Endless|Endless run]]), {{R|The Courier}} will repeatedly restock the [[Merchant]]'s relic offerings with infinite {{R|Circlet|Circlets}}.\n* The [[Merchant]] can occasionally ask the player ''\"Have you seen my courier?\"'' when idling, regardless of whether they possess {{R|The Courier}} or not.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 55: Blur'''\n** Fixed issue where restocked cards via Courier were hard to select using controller.\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** The Courier relic no longer spawns beyond floor 48 (excludes Endless mode).\n** Courier relic description clarified.\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** Colorless Cards mod now correctly interacts with shops. Prevents Courier causing cards to appear in incorrect places on the shop screen.\n* '''Weekly Patch 43: Discovery'''\n** Fixed issue where items restocked via Courier weren't applied discounts.\n* '''Weekly Patch 16: Back to Work'''\n** Relics and Potions in the shop now correctly set their prices when restocked with the Courier.\n* '''Weekly Patch 4: Full speed ahead!'''\n** Discerning Monocle is deprecated until it gets a new effect.\n** Discerning Monocle's price reduction is now an additional effect on the Courier relic.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"2390":{"pageid":2390,"ns":0,"title":"The Specimen","revisions":[{"revid":55950,"parentid":50903,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = The Specimen\n|Image       = TheSpecimen.png\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Character   = Silent\n|Description = Whenever an enemy dies, transfer any {{BD|Poison}} it has to a random enemy.\n|Flavor      = \"Fascinating! I found a mutated creature demonstrating astounding toxic properties. Storing a sample for later examination.\" - Ranwid\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Poison}}{{R|The Specimen}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|character:Silent|Silent-exclusive}} {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Medium Chest]] or [[Large Chest]]\n. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, and {{R|Black Star}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic can be {{R|The Specimen}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|The Specimen}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|The Specimen}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|The Specimen}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|The Specimen}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|The Specimen}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|The Specimen}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|The Specimen}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Colosseum}}: The {{Frame|VICTORY}} option drops 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic, and 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic (which can be {{R|The Specimen}}).\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|The Specimen}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n** {{E|Mind Bloom}}: The {{Frame|I Am War}} option can drop {{R|The Specimen}}.\n** {{E|Mysterious Sphere}}: The {{Frame|Open Sphere}} option can drop {{R|The Specimen}}.\n\n== Spawn Restrictions ==\n* Can only be obtained by [[Silent]].\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Snecko Skull}} will increase the {{BD|Poison}} transferred by 1.\n* The transferred {{BD|Poison}} will trigger the damage from {{C|Sadistic Nature}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If an enemy dies from {{BD|Poison}} damage during their turn, the transferred {{BD|Poison}} will not deal damage this turn even if it is applied to an enemy that hasn't taken {{BD|Poison}} damage yet.\n* If an enemy dies right as {{BD|Poison}} is about to be applied to them (such as from {{C|Poisoned Stab}}, or any {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} with {{C|Envenom}}), the {{BD|Poison}} will not be transferred as the enemy will die before the {{BD|Poison}} is applied.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* If the {{BD|Poison}} is transferred to an enemy with {{BD|Artifact}}, all the {{BD|Poison}} will be lost since the {{BD|Artifact}} will block the {{BD|Poison}} debuff.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{R|The Specimen}} is a reference to the character [https://dorohedoro.fandom.com/wiki/Kaiman Kaiman] from the manga [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dorohedoro ''Dorohedoro''].<ref>https://www.megacrit.com/news/2024-08-07-neowsletter-issue-1#slay-the-spire-trivia-time</ref>\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Specimen relic now uses the same code as other relics for applying its effect.\n* '''Weekly Patch 52: Release Date Price Increase'''\n** Updated relic asset for The Specimen.\n* '''Weekly Patch 47: Metamorphosis'''\n** Fixed issue where The Specimen's Poison transfer failed if the target died before the transfer.\n** Poison transfer target for The Specimen is now seeded random.\n* '''Weekly Patch 19: Seed'''\n** The Specimen relic rarity changed. Boss -> Rare.\n* '''Weekly Patch 17: Patched in the Face'''\n** Fixed issue where Specimen triggering + Exploder Explosion caused a crash.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"3090":{"pageid":3090,"ns":0,"title":"Twisted Funnel","revisions":[{"revid":55989,"parentid":55520,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Twisted Funnel\n|Image       = TwistedFunnel.png\n|Rarity      = Shop\n|Character   = Silent\n|Description = At the start of each combat, apply 4 {{BD|Poison}} to ALL enemies.\n|Flavor      = I wouldn't drink out of it.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Poison}}{{R|Twisted Funnel}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|character:Silent|Silent-exclusive}} {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Shop|Shop}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can only be bought from the [[Merchant]]. Only 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Shop|Shop Relic}} is available per [[Shop]], even with {{R|The Courier}}, since it cannot restock Shop Relics.\n\n== Spawn Restrictions ==\n* Can only be obtained by [[Silent]].\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Order ===\n* Despite \"flashing\" immediately upon entering combat, {{R|Twisted Funnel}} will only apply {{BD|Poison}} after the player has finished drawing their opening hand.\n** {{R|Twisted Funnel}} will even wait to trigger until after additional turn 1 card draw, such as {{R|Ring of the Snake}} and {{R|Bag of Preparation}}.\n* {{R|Twisted Funnel}} will trigger with other \"after opening hand\" relics (such as {{R|Red Mask}} and {{R|Bag of Marbles}}) in pickup order (i.e. from left to right in the player's relic bar).\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Snecko Skull}} will cause {{R|Twisted Funnel}} to apply 5 {{BD|Poison}} to all enemies instead of the normal 4.\n* Starting combat with some {{BD|Poison}} already applied to enemies can effectively increase the damage of other {{BD|Poison}} effects, such as {{C|Poisoned Stab}} and {{C|Crippling Cloud}}.\n* {{R|The Specimen}} may be able to transfer some of {{R|Twisted Funnel}}'s {{BD|Poison}} if an enemy dies before it runs out.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Removes 1 {{BD|Artifact}} from enemies that start combat with some applied, such as the {{M|Sentry|Sentries}} or {{M|Spheric Guardian}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 33: Terror'''\n** Twisted Funnel relic is now Silent only.\n* '''Weekly Patch 32: Face Trader'''\n** Adding shop relic Twisted Funnel.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"1958":{"pageid":1958,"ns":0,"title":"Warped Tongs","revisions":[{"revid":56776,"parentid":51011,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Warped Tongs\n|Image       = WarpedTongs.png\n|Rarity      = Event\n|Source      = Ominous Forge\n|Description = At the start of your turn, {{KW|Upgrade}} a random card in your hand for the rest of combat.\n|Flavor      = The cursed tongs emit a strong desire to return to where they were stolen from.\n|GivesToPlayer = Upgrade\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Upgrade}}{{R|Warped Tongs}} is an {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Event|Event}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\nCan only be obtained from {{E|Ominous Forge}} by selecting the {{Frame|Rummage}} option, where it is acquired alongside {{C|Pain}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n{{R|Warped Tongs}} will always target a card in the player's hand that could still be {{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}}; it will never be \"wasted\" by attempting to {{KW|Upgrade}} a card that is already {{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}} (unless that card is {{C|Searing Blow}} because it can be {{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}} any number of times).\n\n=== Order ===\n* {{R|Warped Tongs}} always waits to trigger until after the player has finished drawing their opening hand.\n<!-- Warped Tongs has the same ordering/timing as Gambling Chip, so if you change this section please also check if the change makes sense to be made for Gambling Chip as well! -->\n* {{R|Warped Tongs}} will always trigger ''after'' the following effects have triggered regardless of whether {{R|Warped Tongs}} was acquired before or after them:\n** {{R|Ring of the Snake}} and {{R|Ring of the Serpent}}\n** {{R|Bag of Preparation}}\n** {{R|Snecko Eye}}\n** {{R|Pure Water}} and {{R|Holy Water}} (the {{C|Miracle|Miracle(s)}} are added to the player's hand first, and may be {{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}})\n** {{R|Bottled Flame}}, {{R|Bottled Lightning}}, and {{R|Bottled Tornado}} (the bottled card may be {{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}})\n** {{R|Ninja Scroll}} (the {{C|Shiv|Shivs}} are added to the player's hand first, and one of them may be {{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}})\n** {{R|Mark of Pain}} (the {{C|Wound|Wounds}} are shuffled into the player's draw pile first)\n** {{R|Enchiridion}} (the free {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} that was added to the player's hand may be {{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}})\n** {{R|Toolbox}} (the player will be prompted to choose 1 of 3 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless cards}} first, and it may be {{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}})\n* {{R|Warped Tongs}} will trigger before or after {{R|Gambling Chip}} depending on their pickup order (i.e. from left to right in the player's relic bar).\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Warped Tongs}} can help curb the player's lack of {{KW|Upgrade|Upgrades}} if they have {{R|Fusion Hammer}} or otherwise find themselves unable to smith often at [[Map Locations#Rest Sites|Rest Sites]].\n* {{C|Searing Blow}} can be {{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}} by {{R|Warped Tongs}} multiple times over the course of a single combat.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If the player has {{R|Snecko Eye}}, {{R|Warped Tongs}} may force an un-{{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}} card's {{KW|Energy}} cost to become its {{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}} cost.\n** For example, if {{R|Snecko Eye}} makes an un-{{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}} {{C|Eruption}} cost 3 {{KW|Energy}}, upgrading it will reduce its cost to 1 (the normal cost of {{C|Eruption}}+) thereby making it cheaper.\n** On the other hand, this can also be a detriment in the opposite scenario. For example, if {{R|Snecko Eye}} makes an un-{{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}} {{C|Barricade}} cost 0 {{KW|Energy}}, upgrading it will increase its cost to 2 (the normal cost of {{C|Barricade}}+) thereby making it more expensive.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* Has no effect if every card in the player's hand is already {{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}}, such as from {{C|Apotheosis}}, {{C|Lesson Learned}}, {{R|Molten Egg}}, {{R|Toxic Egg}}, {{R|Frozen Egg}}, and/or frequent smithing at [[Map Locations#Rest Sites|Rest Sites]].\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{R|Warped Tongs}} is a pair of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tongs tongs] reminiscent of the style used in the practice of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blacksmith blacksmithing]. They're used to hold a piece of metal that would otherwise be too hot to touch with bare hands (or even gloved hands).\n** These kinds of tongs typically only have one circular indent closest to the \"grabbing end\" of the tongs, and {{R|Warped Tongs}} has three such sections all the way up to the pivot point. This could be how {{R|Warped Tongs}} are warped through extended improper use.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Update for Warped Tongs relic description to indicate non-permanent upgrade.\n** Using more noticeable flashy VFX for cards upgraded via Armaments or Warped Tongs.\n** Fixed issue where upgraded card from Warped Tongs wasn't showing the correct value if you had Strength/Dexterity.\n* '''Weekly Patch 41: Chill'''\n** New Event Relic: Warped Tongs.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"2405":{"pageid":2405,"ns":0,"title":"Wrist Blade","revisions":[{"revid":56048,"parentid":56007,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Wrist Blade\n|Image       = WristBlade.png\n|Rarity      = Boss\n|Character   = Silent\n|Description = {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}} that cost 0 deal 4 additional damage.\n|Flavor      = Handy for assassinations.\n}}\n{{R|Wrist Blade}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|character:Silent|Silent-exclusive}} {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Boss|Boss}} [[Relic]]. {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}} that cost 0 {{Icon|GE}}[[Energy]] will deal an additional 4 damage when played. This increase is reflected in the card text during combat.\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be obtained from [[Boss Swap]].\n* After fighting a [[Boss]], {{R|Wrist Blade}} can be offered as a choice of 3 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Boss|Boss Relics}}.\n\n== Spawn Restrictions ==\n* Can only be obtained by [[Silent]].\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Order ===\nWhen calculating damage dealt, all the additive bonuses are added first, and then multiplicative bonuses are multiplied. The final result is rounded down. {{R|Wrist Blade|Wrist Blade's}} damage increase is an additive bonus, behaving similarly to {{BD|Strength}} that only affects specific cards.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* The most obvious gameplay style that synergizes with {{R|Wrist Blade}} is {{C|Shiv|Shivs}}. Each {{C|Shiv}} will deal an additional 4 damage.\n* {{R|Wrist Blade}} will increase the damage of ''any'' {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} that costs 0 for ''any'' reason, even if its normal cost is greater than 0.\n\n==== Effects That Allow Any Attack to Benefit from {{R|Wrist Blade}} ====\n* {{C|Bullet Time}} reduces the cost of all cards in hand to 0.\n* {{C|Setup}} and {{C|Forethought}} reduce the cost of a card to 0 until played.\n* {{C|Swivel}} (if acquired through {{R|Prismatic Shard}} or other means) will cause the next {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} to cost 0.\n* {{C|Madness}} can randomly set an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack's}} cost to 0 for the rest of the combat (or until its cost changes by other means).\n* {{R|Mummified Hand}} can randomly set an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack's}} cost to 0 for the rest of the turn until it's played.\n* {{R|Snecko Eye}} has a 25% chance of randomizing a drawn {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} to cost 0 instead of its normal cost.\n* The {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} generated by {{P|Attack Potion}} will cost 0 if played on the same turn that the [[Potion]] is consumed.\n* {{P|Liquid Memories}} can be used to fetch an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} from the discard pile and set its cost to 0 this turn until played.\n\n==== Silent Attacks That Benefit from {{R|Wrist Blade}} ====\nThe following are {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack&color:Green|Silent Attacks}} (or effects which can easily generate {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}}) that directly benefit from {{R|Wrist Blade}} without needing [[#Effects_That_Allow_Any_Attack_to_Benefit_from_Wrist_Blade|a supporting effect]] to set their cost to 0.\n* {{C|Neutralize}}\n* {{C|Blade Dance|Blade Dance's}} {{C|Shiv|Shivs}}\n* {{C|Cloak and Dagger|Cloak and Dagger's}} {{C|Shiv|Shivs}}\n* {{C|Slice}}\n* {{C|Backstab}}\n* {{C|Endless Agony}}\n* {{C|Infinite Blades|Infinite Blades'}} {{C|Shiv|Shivs}}\n* {{C|Masterful Stab}} (if the player has not lost any HP this combat)\n* {{C|Grand Finale}}\n* {{C|Storm of Steel|Storm of Steel's}} {{C|Shiv|Shivs}}\n* {{P|Cunning Potion|Cunning Potion's}} {{C|Shiv|Shivs+}}\n* The {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} from {{P|Attack Potion}} (when played on the same turn that the [[Potion]] is consumed)\n\n==== Notable Silent Attacks That Can Benefit from {{R|Wrist Blade}} with Support ====\nWhile {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|any Attack in the game}} could theoretically benefit from {{R|Wrist Blade}} if its cost is set to 0, the following are the most notable {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack&color:Green|Silent Attacks}} which benefit more than usual from {{R|Wrist Blade}} if [[#Effects_That_Allow_Any_Attack_to_Benefit_from_Wrist_Blade|a supporting effect]] can set their cost to 0. In particular, cards that hit multiple times will benefit from {{R|Wrist Blade|Wrist Blade's}} damage bonus on each hit.\n* {{C|Bane}} (hits twice if the enemy is {{BD|Poison|Poisoned}})\n* {{C|Dagger Spray}} (hits all enemies twice)\n* {{C|Eviscerate}} (can be discounted to cost 0 by discarding 3 other cards during the turn, and hits 3 times)\n* {{C|Finisher}} (hits multiple times; once per {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} played this turn which can be particularly effective if the player has many other 0-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}} and suitable card draw)\n* {{C|Flechettes}} (hits multiple times; once per {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} in the player's hand)\n* {{C|Riddle with Holes}} (hits 5 times)\n* {{C|Glass Knife}} (hits twice, and its damage reduction will not affect the damage increase from {{R|Wrist Blade}}; effectively meaning it can never deal less than 4 damage per hit)\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{R|Wrist Blade}} is a reference to the iconic [https://assassinscreed.fandom.com/wiki/Hidden_Blade ''Hidden Blade''] item from the Assassin's Creed franchise where it is a common tool for assassinating various enemies in the games.<ref>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assassin%27s_Creed</ref> The visual design, name, and flavor text are direct references to this series.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher (01-14-2020)'''\n** GAMEPLAY: Wrist Blade relic buffed. Additional damage increased from 3 -> 4.\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer (07-01-2019)'''\n** BUG FIX: Fixed Wrist Blade not affecting Sword Boomerang, Rip and Tear, and Thunder Strike.\n* '''Weekly Patch 38: Bane'''\n** Wrist Blade relic now works with cards that are cost 0 via Setup or Forethought.\n* '''Weekly Patch 38: Malaise'''\n** Adding green boss relic Wrist Blade.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]}}}}